    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0387" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72113/606</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jusserand</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 25, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received June 28.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: The Minister of France
                    at Rio asked, jointly with his colleagues of England and Belgium, several weeks
                    ago, the Brazilian Government to make an engagement that it would <pb
                        facs="0388" n="304" xml:id="pg304"/> not rescind the measures taken with
                    regard to private enemy property, except after consultation with the Allied
                    Powers.</p>
                <p>The Minister of Foreign Affairs of Brazil answered that he had no objection in
                    principle to that proposition, but especially desired to know whether the United
                    States would be disposed to make, in so far as it is concerned, an engagement of
                    the same nature.</p>
                <p>I should be thankful to Your Excellency if you would kindly acquaint me with the
                    views of the Federal Government on the subject.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d321-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d321-f1" n="1" xml:id="d321-f1-content">
                <p>Note in Department file: “It was decided not to reply to this note because it was
                    requested that if our answer was ‘No’ we not reply.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
